  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Political Dialogue and Code of Conduct in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, contract with NIMD.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a subactivity in the collection bemo &quot;Youth Political Dialogue 2025&quot;. This project, funded by the Netherlands and implemented by Netherlands Institute for Multiparty Democracy (NIMD), aims to foster peaceful political participation among Ivorian youth ahead of the 2025 presidential elections. Through inclusive political dialogue, leadership training, and the co-creation of a youth code of conduct, the initiative will empower 150 young political and civil society leaders across the country. The activities of NIMD include the facilitation of dialogue sessions and the writing of a code of conduct between youth political leaders. Desired results include strengthened civic engagement, increased youth participation in politics and reduced risks of violence and polarization. The project contributes to SDGs 16, 10 and 17, and supports national efforts to consolidate democratic governance and social cohesion.
